- tmux keybindings
    - in-session keybindings for tmux
    - prefix: Ctrl+T

    - prefix key
        - Ctrl+T
            - description: Prefix key (replaces default Ctrl+B)
            - tmux: set -g prefix C-t

    - session management
        - Ctrl+T r
            - description: Rename current session
            - tmux: bind r command-prompt -I "#S" "rename-session '%%'"
        - Ctrl+T d
            - description: Detach from session
            - tmux: bind d detach-client

    - pane splitting
        - Ctrl+T \
            - description: Split vertical (left and right)
            - tmux: bind \\ split-window -h -c "#{pane_current_path}"
        - Ctrl+T -
            - description: Split horizontal (top and bottom)
            - tmux: bind - split-window -v -c "#{pane_current_path}"

    - pane navigation (no prefix needed)
        - Ctrl+Left
            - description: Move to left pane
            - tmux: bind -n C-Left select-pane -L
        - Ctrl+Right
            - description: Move to right pane
            - tmux: bind -n C-Right select-pane -R
        - Ctrl+Up
            - description: Move to pane above
            - tmux: bind -n C-Up select-pane -U
        - Ctrl+Down
            - description: Move to pane below
            - tmux: bind -n C-Down select-pane -D

    - pane resizing (no prefix needed)
        - Alt+Left
            - description: Shrink pane left
            - tmux: bind -n M-Left resize-pane -L 2
        - Alt+Right
            - description: Expand pane right
            - tmux: bind -n M-Right resize-pane -R 2
        - Alt+Up
            - description: Shrink pane up
            - tmux: bind -n M-Up resize-pane -U 2
        - Alt+Down
            - description: Expand pane down
            - tmux: bind -n M-Down resize-pane -D 2

    - window management
        - Ctrl+T c
            - description: Create new window
            - tmux: bind c new-window -c "#{pane_current_path}"
        - Ctrl+T ,
            - description: Rename current window
            - tmux: bind , command-prompt -I "#W" "rename-window '%%'"
        - Ctrl+T n
            - description: Next window
            - tmux: bind n next-window
        - Ctrl+T p
            - description: Previous window
            - tmux: bind p previous-window
        - Ctrl+T 0-9
            - description: Switch to window by number
            - note: default tmux behavior

    - pane management
        - Ctrl+T x
            - description: Close current pane (with confirmation)
            - tmux: bind x confirm-before -p "Kill pane? (y/n)" kill-pane
        - Ctrl+T z
            - description: Zoom or unzoom current pane
            - tmux: bind z resize-pane -Z
        - Ctrl+T Space
            - description: Cycle through pane layouts
            - tmux: bind Space next-layout

    - mouse scrolling (no prefix needed)
        - Mouse wheel / Touchpad
            - description: Scroll through terminal history instead of cycling commands
            - tmux: bind -n WheelUpPane if-shell ...
            - note: enters copy mode automatically on scroll up

    - copy mode
        - Ctrl+T [
            - description: Enter copy mode (scroll with arrows, PgUp/PgDn)
            - tmux: bind [ copy-mode

    - help
        - Ctrl+T ?
            - description: Show all tmux keybindings
            - tmux: bind ? list-keys
